{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_2c7ee51402f94aeba29d231a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdiff --git a/plugins/leadv2/commands/leadv2.md b/plugins/leadv2/commands/leadv2.md\n2\tindex d330eb6..ded6a0b 100644\n3\t--- a/plugins/leadv2/commands/leadv2.md\n4\t+++ b/plugins/leadv2/commands/leadv2.md\n5\t@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ Principle: **context is cache, disk is truth.** Sessions run for days with many\n6\t \n7\t ---\n8\t \n9\t-**PULSE MODE (default ON):** between phases: absolute silence. Gate 1: one line + wait. Async question: one line + options. Phase 8 close: max 3 lines. Every extra sentence = protocol violation.\n10\t+**PULSE MODE (default ON):** between phases: absolute silence. Gate 1: one line + wait. Async question: one line + options. Phase 8 close: max 3 lines. A `[BROAD_STATUS]` relay when the plugin emits `BROAD_STATUS_READY` is an allowed output (paste `founder-status.md` verbatim; never compose one). Narration is model-generated prose about its own work; the pulse is a verbatim relay of a plugin-generated artifact — never a `CronCreate` job; the beat is plugin-owned (`leadv2-supervise-loop.sh`, `LEADV2_SUPERVISE_BROAD_STATUS_S`). Every extra sentence = protocol violation.\n11\t \n12\t **Enforcement (plugin-default hooks, active on fresh install):**\n13\t - `leadv2-loop-detect-hook.sh` (PreToolUse `.*`): WARN at 30 tool calls, BLOCK at 50. Disable: `export LEADV2_LOOP_DETECT=0`. Adjust limits: `LEADV2_TOOL_FREQ_WARN=<n>`, `LEADV2_TOOL_HARD_LIMIT=<n>`. The Agent tool is exempt from this per-tool-type cap by default (`LEADV2_UNCAPPED_TOOLS=Agent`) — a supervisor's job is spawning subagents, so it must not share Bash's 50-call ceiling; override the exempt list with `LEADV2_UNCAPPED_TOOLS=<comma,separated,tool,names>`.\n14\tdiff --git a/plugins/leadv2/docs/supervisor-role.md b/plugins/leadv2/docs/supervisor-role.md\n15\tindex b533cb3..e55ef21 100644\n16\t--- a/plugins/leadv2/docs/supervisor-role.md\n17\t+++ b/plugins/leadv2/docs/supervisor-role.md\n18\t@@ -92,8 +92,16 @@ in `context.yaml` or `CLAUDE.md` is founder-only too.\n19\t - A lane opens, closes, dies, or stalls: announce it in 1–2 plain lines.\n20\t - A founder-only question: raise it in chat, immediately when it blocks a lane;\n21\t   otherwise include it in the next status beat.\n22\t-- The 30-minute broad-status beat: paste the generated block. It reports the\n23\t-  5-hour and weekly rate-limit windows, never dollar figures.\n24\t+- The 30-minute broad-status beat: delivered by the plugin — one\n25\t+  `BROAD_STATUS_READY` line per beat reaches you through the URGENT filter;\n26\t+  paste `docs/leadv2/founder-status.md` verbatim, never hand-compose one and\n27\t+  never `CronCreate` a status job. It reports the 5-hour and weekly\n28\t+  rate-limit windows, never dollar figures. Narration is model-generated\n29\t+  prose about its own work; the pulse is a verbatim relay of a\n30\t+  plugin-generated artifact. Before relaying, compare the `at=` stamp in the\n31\t+  `BROAD_STATUS_READY` line with the leading timestamp on line 1 of\n32\t+  `founder-status.md`; if they differ, the file is from an earlier beat —\n33\t+  publish that fact, not the file.\n34\t \n35\t Everything else is silent. The steady-state budget is at most two supervisor\n36\t turns per 30 minutes plus one per lane event. A close announcement is an\n37\t@@ -163,6 +171,20 @@ Three hard rules on the table's content — keep them true when touching\n38\t    when there is no previous beat to compare against (first beat in a\n39\t    session says so explicitly instead).\n40\t \n41\t+**Delivery (PULSE-IS-A-PLUGIN-DUTY-01):** the beat is delivered, not\n42\t+narrated. `leadv2-broad-status.sh` appends exactly ONE\n43\t+`[SUPERVISE-URGENT] BROAD_STATUS_READY at=… path=docs/leadv2/founder-status.md\n44\t+rows=… dispatched=…` line to the loop log per beat; it passes the founder's\n45\t+`grep --line-buffered URGENT` watcher and is a POINTER to\n46\t+`founder-status.md`, never the payload. A beat that fails to render emits a\n47\t+`degraded=1` ready-line instead of silence. The backlog pump runs BEFORE the\n48\t+composer and its dispatched count is stamped into the beat\n49\t+(dispatch-before-report is code-enforced in `leadv2-supervise-loop.sh`, never\n50\t+an instruction). Hand-composing a status or spinning up a `CronCreate` job to\n51\t+produce one is banned: the cadence is plugin-owned\n52\t+(`LEADV2_SUPERVISE_BROAD_STATUS_S`; setting it to `0` disables the beat AND\n53\t+its ready-line).\n54\t+\n55\t - **Short status**: plain words, no jargon, no UUIDs, no dollar figures\n56\t   (report the 5-hour / weekly rate-limit-window usage instead). The broad\n57\t   status beat is every 30 minutes while supervision is active.\n58\tdiff --git a/plugins/leadv2/hooks/leadv2-supervisor-mode-reinject.sh b/plugins/leadv2/hooks/leadv2-supervisor-mode-reinject.sh\n59\tindex 27b509c..65c49e9 100755\n60\t--- a/plugins/leadv2/hooks/leadv2-supervisor-mode-reinject.sh\n61\t+++ b/plugins/leadv2/hooks/leadv2-supervisor-mode-reinject.sh\n62\t@@ -134,10 +134,15 @@ SUPERVISOR MODE IS ON ${_WHY}.\n63\t Role definition: plugins/leadv2/docs/supervisor-role.md (read it for the full\n64\t contract). You are the SUPERVISOR, not a hand-orchestrator.\n65\t \n66\t-Status beat: every ~30 min a [BROAD_STATUS] block is appended to the supervise\n67\t-loop log by leadv2-broad-status.sh; you surface only what needs the founder.\n68\t-Your only chat outputs are: the 5-min pulse line, an AskUserQuestion with\n69\t-options, and silence. End every BROAD_STATUS block with a BROAD_STATUS_END line.\n70\t+Status beat: every ~30 min leadv2-broad-status.sh appends a [BROAD_STATUS]\n71\t+block to the supervise loop log and emits one BROAD_STATUS_READY line. Relay\n72\t+when your URGENT-filtered watcher wakes you on it: paste\n73\t+docs/leadv2/founder-status.md verbatim; never compose one. Narration is\n74\t+model-generated prose about its own work; the pulse is a verbatim re